In .NET 10, `WindowSoftInputModeAdjust.Resize` no longer works because Android deprecated `SOFT_INPUT_ADJUST_RESIZE`. MAUI now uses `KeyboardAutoManagerScroll` by default, but that only scrolls to the focused input — it doesn't shrink your layout like a chat screen needs.

**Recommended approach for .NET 10:**

Use `SOFT_INPUT_ADJUST_PAN` combined with listening to keyboard insets so you can add bottom padding to your layout:

### 1. In `Platforms/Android/MainActivity.cs`:

```csharp
using Android.Views;
using AndroidX.Core.View;
using Microsoft.Maui.Platform;

[Activity(WindowSoftInputMode = SoftInput.AdjustResize)] // still set this as a baseline
public class MainActivity : MauiAppCompatActivity
{
    protected override void OnCreate(Bundle? savedInstanceState)
    {
        base.OnCreate(savedInstanceState);

        // Enable edge-to-edge insets handling
        WindowCompat.SetDecorFitsSystemWindows(Window!, false);
    }
}
```

### 2. Create a custom behavior or handler that reacts to insets:

```csharp
#if ANDROID
using AndroidX.Core.View;
using Microsoft.Maui.Platform;

public static class KeyboardInsetHelper
{
    public static void ListenForKeyboard(this Page page, View bottomBar)
    {
        page.HandlerChanged += (s, e) =>
        {
            if (page.Handler?.PlatformView is Android.Views.View platformView)
            {
                ViewCompat.SetOnApplyWindowInsetsListener(platformView, new InsetListener(bottomBar));
            }
        };
    }

    private class InsetListener : Java.Lang.Object, IOnApplyWindowInsetsListener
    {
        private readonly View _bottomBar;
        public InsetListener(View bottomBar) => _bottomBar = bottomBar;

        public WindowInsetsCompat OnApplyWindowInsets(Android.Views.View v, WindowInsetsCompat insets)
        {
            var imeInsets = insets.GetInsets(WindowInsetsCompat.Type.Ime());
            var navInsets = insets.GetInsets(WindowInsetsCompat.Type.NavigationBars());

            // Apply keyboard height as bottom margin/padding
            _bottomBar.Margin = new Thickness(0, 0, 0, 
                Math.Max(imeInsets.Bottom, navInsets.Bottom) / 
                DeviceDisplay.MainDisplayInfo.Density);

            return insets;
        }
    }
}
#endif
```

### 3. In your chat page:

```csharp
public ChatPage()
{
    InitializeComponent();
#if ANDROID
    this.ListenForKeyboard(InputBar); // your bottom entry/bar
#endif
}
```

### iOS (usually works out of the box)

On iOS, `KeyboardAutoManagerScroll` handles this. If not, set padding similarly using `UIKeyboard.WillShowNotification`.

**TL;DR:** The modern pattern is edge-to-edge + `WindowInsetsCompat.Type.Ime()` to detect keyboard height and adjust your layout padding dynamically.
